.TH LCOS-NOTES-CLI 1 "November 2026" "LCOS Notes 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lcos-notes-cli \- query and modify a local Markdown vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lcos-notes-cli COMMAND VAULT
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
All successful commands emit one UTF-8 JSON value and a newline.
VAULT must be a directory; note arguments are vault-relative .md paths.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B notes VAULT
List notes in path byte order.
.TP
.B links VAULT NOTE
List wikilinks with Unicode line/column positions and resolved paths.
.TP
.B mdlinks VAULT NOTE
List local inline Markdown note links as raw, text, path, heading, line, col and
resolved. Paths are percent-decoded UTF-8; heading is null without a hash.
Images, titles, reference-style and non-local links are excluded.
.TP
.B resolve VAULT SOURCE INNER
Resolve a wikilink's inner text from SOURCE.
.TP
.B switch VAULT QUERY
List up to 50 notes ranked by a case-folded subsequence query.
.TP
.B create VAULT TARGET
Create an empty note or return an existing resolved note.
.TP
.B tags VAULT
List tags, including implicit parents, with descendant-note counts.
Both singular tag: and tags: frontmatter keys are recognized in all supported forms.
.TP
.B tagged VAULT TAG
List notes containing TAG or its nested tags.
.TP
.B find VAULT QUERY [--regex] [--word]
Find up to 500 non-overlapping case-insensitive matches with path, line,
Unicode column and line text. Matches stay within one line, excluding its newline
and final carriage return. Newline queries match nothing. Empty queries are refused.
Options must follow QUERY. --regex uses case-insensitive GLib/PCRE syntax per
line; invalid patterns are refused and empty matches skipped. --word requires
non-letter, non-digit, non-underscore boundaries. Rejected candidates retry one
character after their start; accepted matches continue at their end.
.TP
.B retag VAULT OLD NEW
Rename a tag prefix in inline tags and frontmatter, including descendants.
One leading hash is ignored. Only tag text changes; quotes, punctuation and
other bytes remain. Refuse invalid tags, absent OLD, or NEW nested under OLD.
.TP
.B mentions VAULT NOTE
List whole-word, case-insensitive unlinked mentions of the note basename in
other notes as source, line, col and text. Excludes frontmatter, code and both
note-link syntaxes; rejected candidates retry one character later.
.TP
.B backlinks VAULT NOTE
List incoming wikilinks and Markdown note links from other notes.
.TP
.B rename VAULT OLD NEW
Move a note, folder or attachment and repair affected resolved links in both
syntaxes, preserving other bytes. Folder and attachment NEW paths have no .md
handling; attachments may have no extension when link invariants hold.
Refuse existing destinations, a folder moved inside itself, symlinks under
moved folders and invalid UTF-8 notes under them. Refusals write nothing.
.TP
.B render VAULT NOTE
Render GitHub-flavored Markdown with text, style spans and followable note links. Offsets are zero-based
Unicode code points; ranges exclude their end. Frontmatter and trailing paragraph block IDs are omitted; ranges are clipped.
.TP
.B blocks VAULT NOTE
List Markdown blocks in preorder, including list items and quote children,
excluding document and list nodes; consecutive duplicate start lines are omitted.
Return blocks as objects with line and offset. The line is
1-based in the original file, including removed frontmatter. The offset is a
0-based Unicode code point position in the same text returned by render.
Invalid UTF-8 notes are refused.

.TP
.B tasks VAULT NOTE
List task items as JSON with source line, code point col, checked state and
reading-view box offset. Requires a valid UTF-8 note. GFM tables, task lists and
double-tilde strikethrough are rendered by the shared core.

.SH LINK RULES
Markdown paths resolve relative to the source folder, then the vault root,
trying each path with and without an appended .md. A leading slash uses only
the vault root. Dot segments collapse without escaping the vault. Matching uses
NFC normalization followed by Unicode case folding; exact path bytes win ties.
Name and tag comparisons also normalize to NFC; search text does not.
Rename preserves Markdown link text, heading, angle form and extension preference,
escaping percent and path hashes and, outside angles, spaces and parentheses.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 2 on refusal, with a single refused: reason line on standard error.
Unsafe creation targets and invalid note paths are refused. Invalid UTF-8 notes
are ignored by search, tags and backlinks and refused by render and rename.
.SH HIGHLIGHTS AND IMAGES
.B lcos-notes-cli highlights VAULT NOTE
prints the note's reading-view highlights as a JSON array of start, end and text.
.B render
includes an images array of embedded images, each with its offset in the text and vault-relative path.
.SH UNSUPPORTED
Markdown links with titles or reference syntax, following images and external
links, Markdown image embeds, PDF embeds, attachment viewing, NFC search, settings,
graph view, multiple windows, GFM autolinks and footnotes, package publishing
and signing are outside the supported scope.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lcos-notes (1)


.SH DAILY NOTES, TEMPLATES AND CAPTURE
.B daily VAULT [DATE] [--create]
opens or creates a daily note;
.B dailies VAULT
lists daily notes.
.B templates VAULT
lists templates;
.B template VAULT TEMPLATE TITLE
expands one.
.B create VAULT TARGET --template TEMPLATE
creates from a template.
.B unique VAULT
returns a timestamp target.
.B capture VAULT TEXT [--inbox]
appends a quick capture.
.SH ORGANIZATION
.B props VAULT NOTE
lists supported frontmatter properties.
.B aliases VAULT
lists aliases.
.B headings VAULT NOTE
lists Markdown headings.
.B supersede VAULT OLD NEW
writes reciprocal supersession properties. Each note is saved atomically.

.SH LIMITS
There is no separate move or archive CLI command; use rename for path relocation
or the desktop File menu. Supersede saves each document atomically, not both as
a single transaction. The short CLI usage line is not a complete command list;
this manual and DOCUMENTATION.md include U9/U10 commands.
